      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Phenazine fluorophore based imidazole derivatives (S1 and S2) were synthesized and sensor studies were carried out with various cations. Aggregation induced emission (AIE) was observed selectively for Al3+ among other cations under study in case of both sensors. 1H NMR titration supported the aggregation induced emission of S2 with Al3+. ESI mass spectra successfully confirmed the aggregate formation. SEM images clearly showed the aggregation of receptor induced by Al3+ in a flower-like fashion. AIE probe was successfully applied for bio-imaging of RAW264.7 cells."},
